  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting the resilience of agropastoral communities to foster peace between host, refugee, and returnee in Hodh el Chargui</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Due to the intensification of conflicts at the border with Mali since the beginning of 2024, and particularly since the pastoral lean season (April), an unforeseen and sudden concentration of Mauritanian and Malian transhumants has settled on the Mauritanian side of the border, especially in the Moughataa of Adel Bagrou. Because of the high concentration of livestock in this strategic pastoral area, there is a sudden increase in the shortage of pasture and water, risks to animal health, and the potential for conflicts. Given that this region is very vulnerable economically, socially, and to the impacts of climate change, it is important to provide emergency assistance to agropastoral communities, support agropastoral production, and promote conflict prevention and management mechanisms.</narrative>
  </description>
